1
00:00:08,777 --> 00:00:09,974
What's the meaning of this?

2
00:00:10,057 --> 00:00:12,454
I told you to bring
your girlfriend, didn't I?

3
00:00:12,537 --> 00:00:13,854
Yeah.

4
00:00:13,937 --> 00:00:15,797
Except I don't have a girlfriend.

5
00:00:16,937 --> 00:00:18,474
Huh?

6
00:00:18,557 --> 00:00:20,577
I only said I was seeing someone.

7
00:00:21,937 --> 00:00:23,237
Wait, don't tell me...

8
00:00:25,957 --> 00:00:27,574
Nice to meet you.

9
00:00:27,657 --> 00:00:30,814
I'm Hioki. I'm dating Watarai.

10
00:00:30,897 --> 00:00:32,214
Hold on.

11
00:00:32,297 --> 00:00:33,597
Are you being serious?

12
00:00:34,237 --> 00:00:35,537
Yeah.

13
00:00:39,157 --> 00:00:40,657
Oh, and I have proof, too.

14
00:00:49,917 --> 00:00:52,437
No, that just makes it look even sketchier.

15
00:00:54,897 --> 00:00:56,434
Your name is Hioki, right?

16
00:00:56,517 --> 00:00:57,234
Yes.

17
00:00:57,317 --> 00:00:59,454
Tell me his name.

18
00:00:59,537 --> 00:01:00,914
Watarai.

19
00:01:00,997 --> 00:01:02,297
His first name, too.

20
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,274
Tsu...

21
00:01:04,357 --> 00:01:05,657
Tsukasa.

22
00:01:06,837 --> 00:01:08,174
Then...

23
00:01:08,257 --> 00:01:09,873
Then what middle school
did Tsukasa graduate from?

24
00:01:09,897 --> 00:01:11,034
Huh?

25
00:01:11,117 --> 00:01:11,874
I don't know.

26
00:01:11,957 --> 00:01:13,534
What club was he in back then?

27
00:01:13,617 --> 00:01:14,354
I don't know.

28
00:01:14,437 --> 00:01:15,737
His blood type?

29
00:01:16,857 --> 00:01:17,634
I don't know.

30
00:01:17,717 --> 00:01:19,017
His favorite food?

31
00:01:23,357 --> 00:01:24,797
You don't know anything about him!

32
00:01:26,057 --> 00:01:27,357
I'm sorry.

33
00:01:28,017 --> 00:01:30,354
So what are you two playing at?

34
00:01:30,437 --> 00:01:32,014
Actually trying to trick me.

35
00:01:32,097 --> 00:01:33,874
We're not tricking you.

36
00:01:33,957 --> 00:01:35,437
Well, it's just weird!

37
00:01:37,577 --> 00:01:38,877
Weird?

38
00:01:40,677 --> 00:01:42,234
No...

39
00:01:42,317 --> 00:01:43,834
I mean...

40
00:01:43,917 --> 00:01:46,437
It's just a lot to wrap my head around.

41
00:01:47,057 --> 00:01:48,357
Were you actually...

42
00:01:48,937 --> 00:01:50,537
into guys from the very beginning?

43
00:01:51,377 --> 00:01:54,034
Like, was dating me just
a cover-up or something?

44
00:01:54,117 --> 00:01:55,417
It wasn't like that.

45
00:01:57,057 --> 00:01:58,357
Then why?

46
00:01:58,977 --> 00:02:01,094
Are you just messing with me?

47
00:02:01,177 --> 00:02:03,677
Cut it out with this stupid joke.

48
00:02:06,057 --> 00:02:07,637
Stupid?

49
00:02:09,797 --> 00:02:11,097
Besides...

50
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:13,817
aren't you the one messing around here?

51
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:18,155
What do you even know, Suzu?

52
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:19,640
Watarai...

53
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:26,197
You have no idea... how hard
I tried just to be with Hioki.

54
00:02:28,237 --> 00:02:29,537
Fine.

55
00:02:30,077 --> 00:02:31,397
Maybe I don't.

56
00:02:32,457 --> 00:02:33,545
However...

57
00:02:34,717 --> 00:02:36,397
at the very least...

58
00:02:37,103 --> 00:02:39,083
I know Tsukasa way better than he does.

59
00:02:40,357 --> 00:02:41,434
What?

60
00:02:41,517 --> 00:02:43,034
Because this is ridiculous!

61
00:02:43,117 --> 00:02:45,637
He claims to be your boyfriend,
yet he knows nothing about you.

62
00:02:50,657 --> 00:02:51,957
Forget it.

63
00:02:53,297 --> 00:02:54,394
If you don't believe us,

64
00:02:55,092 --> 00:02:56,137
suit yourself.

65
00:02:57,137 --> 00:02:58,437
Still...

66
00:02:59,197 --> 00:03:01,037
Hioki is the one I love.

67
00:03:03,577 --> 00:03:04,877
Hioki, let's go.

68
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:08,580
Hioki.

69
00:03:26,337 --> 00:03:27,637
I'm really sorry.

70
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:30,646
I shouldn't have put you through that.

71
00:03:32,797 --> 00:03:34,097
No.

72
00:03:35,457 --> 00:03:36,877
I'm the one who should apologize.

73
00:03:38,237 --> 00:03:40,217
You have nothing to apologize for, Hioki.

74
00:03:42,217 --> 00:03:43,517
But...

75
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:48,745
Is it bothering you that you
couldn't answer those questions?

76
00:03:57,137 --> 00:03:58,557
Don't worry about it.

77
00:03:59,597 --> 00:04:04,010
None of that stuff... is anything
you really need to know anyway.

78
00:04:08,677 --> 00:04:10,377
Do you like me, Hioki?

79
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:14,157
I do.

80
00:04:17,297 --> 00:04:18,936
Then that's enough.

81
00:04:20,657 --> 00:04:23,077
As long as you like me,

82
00:04:23,817 --> 00:04:25,117
that's all I need.

83
00:04:27,797 --> 00:04:29,637
So don't make that face.

84
00:04:30,337 --> 00:04:31,637
Come on, let's go.

85
00:04:39,217 --> 00:04:40,717
I always felt the same way.

86
00:04:42,697 --> 00:04:43,997
Until...

87
00:04:44,937 --> 00:04:46,634
Are you being serious?

88
00:04:46,717 --> 00:04:48,197
Well, it's just weird!

89
00:04:58,817 --> 00:05:00,117
That day,

90
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,035
for the first time, I felt like...

91
00:05:02,737 --> 00:05:04,837
reality had hit me right in the face.

92
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:07,974
"School Trip: Joined a Group I'm Not Close to Season2"

93
00:06:08,057 --> 00:06:09,669
Two weeks have passed since then.

94
00:06:09,752 --> 00:06:11,446
(Episode 5: Future)

95
00:06:18,837 --> 00:06:20,781
Excuse me, coming through.

96
00:06:22,657 --> 00:06:24,259
No running in the halls!

97
00:06:30,637 --> 00:06:31,937
Watarai.

98
00:06:32,617 --> 00:06:34,394
Oh, hey, Hioki.

99
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:35,374
I'm heading out.

100
00:06:35,457 --> 00:06:36,757
Yeah.

101
00:06:40,557 --> 00:06:41,557
Did you come to get me?

102
00:06:41,597 --> 00:06:43,014
Yeah.

103
00:06:43,097 --> 00:06:44,433
We're having lunch together, right?

104
00:06:44,457 --> 00:06:45,714
Yeah.

105
00:06:45,797 --> 00:06:49,574
Oh, I didn't bring lunch today,
so I have to hit the school store.

106
00:06:49,657 --> 00:06:51,357
You can go ahead and eat with the others.

107
00:06:52,597 --> 00:06:54,837
Mind if I tag along with you?

108
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:56,894
Huh?

109
00:06:56,977 --> 00:06:59,194
Even though you brought your lunch?

110
00:06:59,277 --> 00:07:00,214
Yeah.

111
00:07:00,297 --> 00:07:01,597
Well...

112
00:07:02,177 --> 00:07:03,717
I just want to be with you.

113
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:09,679
Hioki seems a little different lately.

114
00:07:11,297 --> 00:07:11,865
Let's go.

115
00:07:11,948 --> 00:07:12,948
Yeah.

116
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:19,874
Sorry to keep you waiting.

117
00:07:19,957 --> 00:07:21,074
Oh, not at all.

118
00:07:21,157 --> 00:07:22,314
What did you get?

119
00:07:22,397 --> 00:07:25,674
Melon bread, a chocolate
cornet, and yakisoba bread.

120
00:07:25,757 --> 00:07:26,974
Looks good.

121
00:07:27,057 --> 00:07:30,797
By the way, Watarai, what's
your favorite kind of bread?

122
00:07:31,597 --> 00:07:33,594
Huh? Let's see...

123
00:07:33,677 --> 00:07:34,734
Melon bread, maybe?

124
00:07:34,817 --> 00:07:35,894
Oh...

125
00:07:35,977 --> 00:07:37,617
What about rice balls?

126
00:07:40,517 --> 00:07:42,214
Hioki.

127
00:07:42,297 --> 00:07:43,977
Don't tell me it's still bothering you.

128
00:07:44,837 --> 00:07:46,474
What is?

129
00:07:46,557 --> 00:07:47,857
What Suzu said.

130
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:50,437
What? No, it's not.

131
00:07:52,537 --> 00:07:54,297
Oh, it totally is.

132
00:07:54,977 --> 00:07:56,937
Guess Hioki's got a cute side too.

133
00:07:58,177 --> 00:07:59,697
Yeah, it is cute.

134
00:08:01,997 --> 00:08:04,177
I mean, Hioki's always cute.

135
00:08:05,917 --> 00:08:07,154
Still,

136
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:09,357
you really don't need to sweat that stuff.

137
00:08:10,857 --> 00:08:12,659
How could it not bother me?

138
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:17,831
I was completely useless back
there. I couldn't even argue back.

139
00:08:20,277 --> 00:08:23,057
And I hate myself for never even
trying to learn more about him.

140
00:08:24,317 --> 00:08:27,457
I get why it's bugging you,

141
00:08:28,377 --> 00:08:29,674
but just let it go.

142
00:08:29,757 --> 00:08:31,177
It's in the past anyway.

143
00:08:31,777 --> 00:08:33,677
Don't waste your energy on an ex.

144
00:08:34,197 --> 00:08:36,034
You have a point, I guess.

145
00:08:36,117 --> 00:08:39,353
Didn't Watarai say he wouldn't
see his ex anymore, anyway?

146
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:40,854
Yeah, well...

147
00:08:41,537 --> 00:08:44,294
she might not be over him yet.

148
00:08:44,377 --> 00:08:45,937
Is she still reaching out to him?

149
00:08:46,937 --> 00:08:48,987
No, well...

150
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:50,363
I wouldn't know.

151
00:08:50,917 --> 00:08:52,297
I blocked her.

152
00:08:53,217 --> 00:08:54,517
Blocked her?

153
00:08:55,797 --> 00:08:57,134
Yeah.

154
00:08:57,217 --> 00:08:58,777
Way to go, Tsukasa.

155
00:08:59,557 --> 00:09:03,337
Wait, for someone like
Watarai to go that far...

156
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,504
he must have been really mad, huh?

157
00:09:05,587 --> 00:09:07,647
Not so much mad...

158
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,799
More like it really stung.

159
00:09:11,097 --> 00:09:12,454
To tell you the truth,

160
00:09:12,537 --> 00:09:13,957
I kind of got my hopes up.

161
00:09:15,117 --> 00:09:16,417
Your hopes up?

162
00:09:17,477 --> 00:09:19,437
I figured if I explained
everything face-to-face,

163
00:09:19,857 --> 00:09:21,917
maybe she'd accept it.

164
00:09:25,137 --> 00:09:27,697
Then again, maybe her
reaction is normal.

165
00:09:38,037 --> 00:09:39,337
I see.

166
00:09:39,997 --> 00:09:41,974
Yeah, that's definitely rough.

167
00:09:42,057 --> 00:09:43,125
Yeah.

168
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:45,602
Watarai's been looking
a bit down lately, too.

169
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,597
In that case,

170
00:09:51,197 --> 00:09:54,219
why don't we all go blow
off some steam for a change?

171
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,345
Huh?

172
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:56,428
That's a great idea.

173
00:09:56,497 --> 00:09:57,797
Count me in.

174
00:09:58,697 --> 00:09:59,997
Blow off some steam?

175
00:10:00,617 --> 00:10:01,974
Doing... doing what?

176
00:10:02,057 --> 00:10:03,417
Hmm...

177
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:06,731
How about...

178
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:13,297
Bowling, huh?

179
00:10:13,937 --> 00:10:15,797
It's been ages since I last bowled.

180
00:10:17,337 --> 00:10:21,054
Finals are right around the corner. Shouldn't
you guys be taking college prep seriously?

181
00:10:21,137 --> 00:10:22,194
Who cares?

182
00:10:22,277 --> 00:10:24,414
Even seniors need a breather.

183
00:10:24,497 --> 00:10:25,354
Get off me.

184
00:10:25,437 --> 00:10:27,914
Watarai, are you good at bowling?

185
00:10:27,997 --> 00:10:29,814
Well, hard to say.

186
00:10:29,897 --> 00:10:31,397
It's been forever for me, too.

187
00:10:32,217 --> 00:10:33,594
What about you, Hioki?

188
00:10:33,677 --> 00:10:34,714
I'm average.

189
00:10:34,797 --> 00:10:36,177
Not great, not terrible.

190
00:10:37,337 --> 00:10:38,074
Gotcha.

191
00:10:38,157 --> 00:10:39,554
So, how are we doing this?

192
00:10:39,637 --> 00:10:40,937
Team match?

193
00:10:41,677 --> 00:10:42,454
Sounds good.

194
00:10:42,537 --> 00:10:44,519
Hold everything!

195
00:10:45,697 --> 00:10:47,814
If it's a match you want...

196
00:10:52,217 --> 00:10:54,114
we'll gladly take you on!

197
00:10:54,197 --> 00:10:57,177
Oh, you guys finally showed up.

198
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:06,174
(Badminton Club VS The Big Four)

199
00:11:06,257 --> 00:11:07,594
Bring it on!

200
00:11:07,677 --> 00:11:09,657
Let's settle this once and for all...

201
00:11:10,297 --> 00:11:11,794
and see who the real Big Four are!

202
00:11:11,877 --> 00:11:13,857
Time to dethrone the kings?

203
00:11:14,377 --> 00:11:15,094
Now I'm getting fired up!

204
00:11:15,177 --> 00:11:16,714
Come on, there's no way we can win.

205
00:11:16,797 --> 00:11:17,933
Yeah, I don't see us winning at all.

206
00:11:17,957 --> 00:11:18,894
Quit muttering over there.

207
00:11:18,977 --> 00:11:19,679
Let's get this started already!

208
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:22,348
Right...

209
00:11:24,277 --> 00:11:26,757
Man, I really wanted to be on Hioki's team.

210
00:11:27,257 --> 00:11:28,834
Quit whining, Watarai.

211
00:11:28,917 --> 00:11:31,597
Yeah, rock-paper-scissors
decided it fair and square.

212
00:11:33,157 --> 00:11:34,714
Still...

213
00:11:34,797 --> 00:11:36,257
He's my Hioki, though.

214
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,574
It's okay.

215
00:11:40,657 --> 00:11:42,754
I'm all yours, Watarai.

216
00:11:42,837 --> 00:11:44,154
So be a good boy.

217
00:11:44,237 --> 00:11:45,537
Okay?

218
00:11:46,137 --> 00:11:48,708
Hioki totally has Watarai
wrapped around his finger.

219
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:51,836
It's seriously like an
owner and his giant puppy.

220
00:11:53,057 --> 00:11:55,048
Hey, Hioki!

221
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:57,257
Quit flirting with Mr. Handsome over there.

222
00:11:58,051 --> 00:11:59,344
Keep your eyes

223
00:11:59,997 --> 00:12:01,574
on my special

224
00:12:01,657 --> 00:12:03,194
miracle pitch!

225
00:12:03,277 --> 00:12:04,277
Got it!

226
00:12:08,137 --> 00:12:09,437
There it goes!

227
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:29,237
Yeah! Awesome!

228
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:32,627
So sweet.

229
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,545
Awesome!

230
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:01,948
As long as I'm with Hioki,

231
00:13:02,917 --> 00:13:04,217
honestly, nothing else

232
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:06,217
really matters.

233
00:13:07,245 --> 00:13:08,454
Ah, dang it!

234
00:13:14,294 --> 00:13:15,729
It's been ages since I've
done this. This is a blast.

235
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:18,617
Yeah, and being with
you makes it even better.

236
00:13:20,957 --> 00:13:22,257
Reality,

237
00:13:23,097 --> 00:13:24,397
the rest of the world,

238
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:26,639
or the future...

239
00:13:27,837 --> 00:13:29,874
All of those things

240
00:13:29,957 --> 00:13:32,395
suddenly feel completely trivial.

241
00:13:34,337 --> 00:13:36,274
I'm just overwhelmingly happy,

242
00:13:38,477 --> 00:13:39,754
Whoa!

243
00:13:39,837 --> 00:13:41,117
and cherish every single moment.

244
00:13:41,197 --> 00:13:42,497
Nice!

245
00:13:43,997 --> 00:13:45,354
For you.

246
00:13:45,437 --> 00:13:46,154
Wait, really?

247
00:13:46,237 --> 00:13:48,017
Yeah, I don't need it.

248
00:13:48,745 --> 00:13:50,494
Thanks. Let's share it later, then.

249
00:13:50,577 --> 00:13:51,294
Sure.

250
00:13:51,377 --> 00:13:53,654
Besides Hioki,

251
00:13:53,737 --> 00:13:55,037
I don't need a single thing.

252
00:13:56,637 --> 00:13:57,937
Today was really fun.

253
00:14:01,617 --> 00:14:02,917
Even so...

254
00:14:04,057 --> 00:14:05,834
Um, excuse me.

255
00:14:05,917 --> 00:14:07,054
Did you drop this?

256
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:07,854
Oh, I did!

257
00:14:07,937 --> 00:14:08,937
Thank you so much.

258
00:14:08,997 --> 00:14:09,714
No problem at all.

259
00:14:09,797 --> 00:14:10,534
Sorry about that.

260
00:14:10,617 --> 00:14:11,917
That thing looks awesome.

261
00:14:14,677 --> 00:14:16,497
I wonder how Hioki feels.

262
00:14:19,057 --> 00:14:21,037
In the future he pictures for himself,

263
00:14:22,217 --> 00:14:23,817
maybe I'm not even in it.

264
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,234
Oh, here it is.

265
00:14:38,317 --> 00:14:39,617
Sorry for the wait.

266
00:14:41,497 --> 00:14:45,014
By the way, did you guys turn in
your college preference forms yet?

267
00:14:45,097 --> 00:14:46,194
Not yet.

268
00:14:46,277 --> 00:14:47,957
I'm still torn on what major to pick.

269
00:14:49,217 --> 00:14:50,873
Hotta, you're aiming
for agriculture, right?

270
00:14:50,897 --> 00:14:51,974
Yeah.

271
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:54,497
Haven't narrowed down
which school yet, though.

272
00:14:56,237 --> 00:14:57,914
I already turned mine in.

273
00:14:57,997 --> 00:14:58,714
Seriously?

274
00:14:58,797 --> 00:14:59,374
Yep.

275
00:14:59,457 --> 00:15:00,514
Something music-related?

276
00:15:00,597 --> 00:15:02,477
Nah, just a regular four-year university.

277
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:06,577
As much as I love music,

278
00:15:07,217 --> 00:15:09,577
realistically, making a living
out of it is just too tough.

279
00:15:10,617 --> 00:15:11,917
Makes sense.

280
00:15:12,977 --> 00:15:14,454
What about you, Hioki?

281
00:15:14,537 --> 00:15:15,977
Have you narrowed down your choices?

282
00:15:16,337 --> 00:15:17,917
Yeah, I have a few places in mind.

283
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,153
Somewhere you can commute to from home?

284
00:15:19,177 --> 00:15:19,894
Yeah.

285
00:15:19,977 --> 00:15:22,017
Though I'm actually planning
to move out on my own.

286
00:15:22,137 --> 00:15:23,674
Wait, really?

287
00:15:23,757 --> 00:15:25,050
Live by yourself?

288
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:27,357
Yeah, I figure it'd be
a good life experience.

289
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:31,437
I see.

290
00:15:32,477 --> 00:15:34,034
How about Watarai?

291
00:15:34,117 --> 00:15:34,834
Me?

292
00:15:34,917 --> 00:15:37,177
You're probably fine going
wherever Hioki goes, right?

293
00:15:38,377 --> 00:15:39,934
Pretty much.

294
00:15:40,017 --> 00:15:41,554
That's the plan.

295
00:15:41,637 --> 00:15:44,397
Well, if you don't have anything
specific you wanna do, why not?

296
00:15:45,137 --> 00:15:46,437
Something I want to do...

297
00:15:48,137 --> 00:15:50,273
You two are totally gonna be all
lovey-dovey on campus, though...

298
00:15:50,297 --> 00:15:50,950
100 percent.

299
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:51,814
Right?

300
00:15:51,897 --> 00:15:52,594
Nothing wrong with that, though.

301
00:15:52,677 --> 00:15:53,974
Whoa, it talked! Creepy!

302
00:15:54,057 --> 00:15:55,433
Exams are right around the corner, huh?

303
00:15:55,457 --> 00:15:57,394
Ugh, talk about depressing.

304
00:15:57,477 --> 00:15:58,634
Exams, man...

305
00:15:58,717 --> 00:16:01,377
Hey, once they're over, it's summer break!

306
00:16:01,897 --> 00:16:03,817
Should we take a trip
somewhere again this year?

307
00:16:03,897 --> 00:16:05,074
Wanna ask Ryoto?

308
00:16:05,157 --> 00:16:05,874
Ooh, good idea.

309
00:16:05,957 --> 00:16:07,034
Right?

310
00:16:07,117 --> 00:16:09,510
Come on, Morisaki, ask him...

311
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:13,614
I don't have a dream,

312
00:16:13,697 --> 00:16:15,408
or anyone I aspire to be.

313
00:16:16,537 --> 00:16:17,837
All I want...

314
00:16:25,057 --> 00:16:26,357
Sorry.

315
00:16:26,857 --> 00:16:29,757
I've gotta run somewhere.
You guys head back without me.

316
00:16:43,926 --> 00:16:47,086
[Linkage English Syntax]

317
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:54,238
Watarai?

318
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,559
Hioki.

319
00:16:57,642 --> 00:16:58,643
Is everything okay?

320
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,277
Yeah, it's nothing major.

321
00:17:00,857 --> 00:17:02,157
Where are the others?

322
00:17:02,977 --> 00:17:04,334
They already went home.

323
00:17:04,417 --> 00:17:05,417
Gotcha.

324
00:17:05,457 --> 00:17:06,974
Yeah.

325
00:17:07,057 --> 00:17:10,780
Hioki, do you know which
college you want to go to?

326
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,771
I've narrowed it down to a few.

327
00:17:14,877 --> 00:17:18,898
Then... is there anything
you want to do in the future?

328
00:17:19,637 --> 00:17:20,937
Huh?

329
00:17:21,516 --> 00:17:23,534
Well, let's see...

330
00:17:23,617 --> 00:17:25,137
Nothing specific really comes to mind.

331
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:29,299
I've got my hands full just
studying for entrance exams,

332
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:32,109
so I figured I'd worry
about that once I get in.

333
00:17:32,777 --> 00:17:34,077
I see.

334
00:17:38,697 --> 00:17:39,874
What about you, Watarai?

335
00:17:39,957 --> 00:17:41,477
Do you have any dreams for the future?

336
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:44,855
More than a dream,

337
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:47,608
there is one wish I want to come true.

338
00:17:48,557 --> 00:17:49,857
What is it?

339
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:52,296
All I want...

340
00:17:52,897 --> 00:17:54,197
is to stay with you

341
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:56,200
for the rest of our lives.

342
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:00,596
is to live a happy life.

343
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,214
A happy life, huh?

344
00:18:04,297 --> 00:18:05,594
Yeah.

345
00:18:05,677 --> 00:18:07,454
What kind of life do you have in mind?

346
00:18:07,537 --> 00:18:08,837
Huh?

347
00:18:09,964 --> 00:18:11,549
Like, say...

348
00:18:18,917 --> 00:18:21,214
living in an apartment like this one.

349
00:18:21,297 --> 00:18:22,597
Whoa...

350
00:18:23,417 --> 00:18:25,396
Rent for a place like that looks pricey.

351
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:26,772
True.

352
00:18:27,537 --> 00:18:28,674
What about you, Hioki?

353
00:18:28,757 --> 00:18:30,413
What kind of place
would you want to live in?

354
00:18:30,742 --> 00:18:31,213
Me?

355
00:18:31,237 --> 00:18:32,514
Yeah.

356
00:18:32,597 --> 00:18:33,693
Even if it's totally unrealistic?

357
00:18:33,717 --> 00:18:34,614
Of course.

358
00:18:34,697 --> 00:18:36,254
Dreaming is free, right?

359
00:18:36,337 --> 00:18:37,637
Fair point.

360
00:18:38,297 --> 00:18:39,910
Let's see...

361
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:45,041
Oh, something like this.

362
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,753
Wait, you want to live
in a luxury high-rise?

363
00:18:46,777 --> 00:18:48,177
No, look.

364
00:18:49,237 --> 00:18:51,589
I just think having a great
view would be amazing.

365
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:52,798
Anything else?

366
00:18:53,417 --> 00:18:54,968
Oh,

367
00:18:55,051 --> 00:18:57,345
plenty of closet space would be nice, too.

368
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:00,154
Let me see...

369
00:19:00,237 --> 00:19:01,537
Ah, kind of like this.

370
00:19:02,058 --> 00:19:04,101
Whoa, that's huge.

371
00:19:04,917 --> 00:19:10,537
I don't have that many clothes,
though I bet you have tons, Watarai.

372
00:19:13,317 --> 00:19:14,988
Wait...

373
00:19:15,071 --> 00:19:16,404
Hmm?

374
00:19:16,487 --> 00:19:17,787
Huh?

375
00:19:18,417 --> 00:19:19,717
Wait, do you mean...

376
00:19:20,257 --> 00:19:22,137
Oh, sorry. Do you not
actually have that many?

377
00:19:22,717 --> 00:19:24,197
That's not what I meant.

378
00:19:25,657 --> 00:19:26,957
Everything you just said...

379
00:19:28,497 --> 00:19:30,977
were you picturing the
two of us living together?

380
00:19:33,281 --> 00:19:34,674
Wasn't that the idea?

381
00:19:35,517 --> 00:19:39,374
Well, earlier you said you
wanted to live on your own.

382
00:19:39,457 --> 00:19:43,757
Oh, right. I just meant
while I'm in college.

383
00:19:47,077 --> 00:19:48,377
So...

384
00:19:48,977 --> 00:19:50,377
after we graduate,

385
00:19:51,777 --> 00:19:54,277
you'd want to move in with me?

386
00:19:55,737 --> 00:19:57,013
Yeah, that's what I was thinking.

387
00:19:57,037 --> 00:19:58,394
Oh, unless you don't want to...

388
00:19:58,477 --> 00:19:59,957
Are you kidding? Of course I want to!

389
00:20:02,737 --> 00:20:04,037
Honestly,

390
00:20:04,704 --> 00:20:07,104
this might be the happiest
I've ever been in my entire life.

391
00:20:08,887 --> 00:20:10,986
- Are you for real?
- Yeah.

392
00:20:15,377 --> 00:20:19,385
Still, to actually
afford a place like this,

393
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:22,305
we'd have to make a ton of money, huh?

394
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:23,681
Don't worry.

395
00:20:24,577 --> 00:20:26,957
I'll work hard enough
to earn for the both of us.

396
00:20:29,137 --> 00:20:30,437
Huh?

397
00:20:31,443 --> 00:20:34,903
Whatever you want,
Hioki, I'll buy it all for you.

398
00:20:35,497 --> 00:20:36,934
Whoa...

399
00:20:37,017 --> 00:20:38,317
Thanks.

400
00:20:38,821 --> 00:20:40,654
Guess I have a lot to
look forward to, then.

401
00:20:40,737 --> 00:20:42,077
You bet you do.

402
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,245
Wait, no, I was just kidding!

403
00:20:47,317 --> 00:20:48,181
Well, I'm dead serious.

404
00:20:48,264 --> 00:20:49,264
Huh?

405
00:20:53,257 --> 00:20:54,954
What you said earlier...

406
00:20:55,037 --> 00:20:56,506
can I hold you to it?

407
00:20:56,582 --> 00:20:59,247
Wait, I told you I was joking...

408
00:20:59,337 --> 00:21:01,037
Not the part about the money.

409
00:21:01,597 --> 00:21:03,763
I mean the part about us
living together someday.

410
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:06,927
Oh. Yeah, of course I meant that.

411
00:21:08,077 --> 00:21:09,617
Then it's a promise.

412
00:21:10,177 --> 00:21:11,604
Okay.

413
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,267
It's a promise.

414
00:21:18,557 --> 00:21:19,857
Thank you.

415
00:21:20,697 --> 00:21:23,637
Thanks to you, Hioki, a lot
of things just clicked for me.

416
00:21:24,997 --> 00:21:26,254
Did I actually help?

417
00:21:26,337 --> 00:21:27,994
Yeah.

418
00:21:28,077 --> 00:21:29,377
You really did.

419
00:21:30,657 --> 00:21:31,957
Thank you.

420
00:21:33,637 --> 00:21:34,937
Now,

421
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:37,313
I won't hesitate anymore.

422
00:21:41,817 --> 00:21:43,514
Shall we go?

423
00:21:43,597 --> 00:21:44,897
Yeah.

424
00:22:05,950 --> 00:22:09,662
As long as I'm in Hioki's future,

425
00:22:10,477 --> 00:22:12,498
all I have to do now is
keep moving forward.

426
00:22:26,166 --> 00:22:28,306
[Various university entrance exam books]

427
00:22:35,177 --> 00:22:36,477
For Hioki,

428
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:38,983
I...

429
00:22:41,717 --> 00:22:43,654
No matter what the dream is,

430
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:45,489
I'll make it a reality.

431
00:22:56,117 --> 00:22:58,461
(Next Episode Preview)
Here it comes, here it comes!

432
00:22:58,544 --> 00:23:00,653
(The Last Summer Break of High
School) What do I do, what do I do?

433
00:23:00,677 --> 00:23:01,834
Say cheese.

434
00:23:01,917 --> 00:23:05,054
I'm so crazy about you right now, I
don't know what to do with myself.

435
00:23:05,137 --> 00:23:07,094
Well, I like you way more.

436
00:23:07,177 --> 00:23:10,914
Actually, there's something I
need to tell you. (Determination.)

437
00:23:10,997 --> 00:23:13,084
Bug, bug, bug...
